3. **Insocrine response**: The kidneys become more sensitive to the release of the hormone lipulinin, which is released in response to increased blood pressure. This stimulates the release of the hormone-binding factor (FBB). FBB is released in response to increased blood pressure, which stimulates the release of the hormone-binding factor (FBB). FBB is repeated again to maintain blood pressure homeostasis.

