What is the name of the reaction in which toluene is oxidized to benzaldehyde using chromyl chloride?<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","The reaction in which toluene is oxidized to benzaldehyde using chromyl chloride (CrOCl₃) is known as the **Sandens-Kohllschscher reaction**. 

The reaction involves the oxidation of an aromatic ketone (e.g., toluene) to an α-hydroxy ketone (a ketonone) using chromyl chloride in the presence of a catalyst like sulfuric acid. The α-hydroxy compound is then hydrolyzed to form the corresponding aldehyde. 

