","The third law of thermodynamics states that the entropy of a perfect crystal at absolute zero is zero. This is because perfect crystals have perfect translational, molecular, and electronic order. At absolute zero, all of these degrees of freedom are unoccupied, resulting in no disorder and thus no entropy.

