The observed effects of the reaction are as follows:

1. The salt (NaHCO₃) is soluble in water, so the reaction will be a homogeneous reaction, meaning it will be in an aqueous solution.
2. The reaction will release heat, which is an exothermic process. This will result in an increase in the temperature of the solution.
3. The solution will become more neutral as the reaction proceeds, as the excess acid and base are neutralized.

The fully ionized equation for the reaction between solid benzoic acid (H(C₇H₅O₂)) and sodium hydroxide (NaOH) is:

H(C₇H₅O₂) + NaOH → CH₃COO⁻Na⁺ + H₂O
