2H2(g) + O2(g) → 2H2O(l)

We can use the standard Gibbs free energy of formation (ΔGf) values to find the total Gibbs free energy change (ΔG) for the reaction.

ΔG = [2 × ΔGf(H2O)] - [2 × ΔGf(H2) + ΔGf(O2)]

