ΔG = -474.2 kJ/mol * 2 moles = -948.4 kJ

So, the change in Gibbs free energy for the reaction of 2 moles of hydrogen gas with 1 mole of oxygen gas at a constant temperature of 298 K and a pressure of 1 bar is -948.4 kJ.
