\[
\lambda_c = \frac{2\pi}{k_f}
\]  
where \(k_f\) is the free-field propagation angle (Fresel constant) of the incident light.  

The Fresnel constant is related to the difference in refractive indices:  
\[
\frac{n_{\text{eff}} - n_f}{n_{\text{eff}} + n_f} = \frac{n_{\text{air}} - n_{\text{film}}}{n_{\text{air}} + n_{\text{film}}}
\]  
where \(n_{\text{eff}}\) is the effective index of the slab, \(n_f\) is the refractive index of the cladding, and \(n_{\text{air}}\) is the refractive index of air (approximately 1).  

Given \(n_{\text{eff}} - n_f \sim 0.3\), we can rearrange the above equation to solve for \(n_{\text{eff}} + n_f\):  
\[
n_{\text{eff}} + n_f = \frac{2n_f}{1 - (n_{\text{eff}} - n_f)}
\]  
Substituting \(n_{\text{eff}} - n_f = 0.3\):  
\[
n_{\text{eff}} + n_f = \frac{2n_f}{1 - 0.3} = \frac{2n_f}{0.7} \approx 2.857n_f
\]  
